],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.465,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Only 'config_key and feature_flag names are section-qualified as <section>.<key>' is stated","'ci_gate' detection is 'scripts/check_*.py + workflow run: steps' with count 280 (29 + 251) — two source shapes, no stated naming rule for either","AC1 asserts name-set disjointness but the name derivation for 5 of 7 kinds is implicit"],"finding":"The per-(kind,name) naming scheme is specified only for config_key and feature_flag (section-qualified <section>.<key>). The naming rule for lock, env_var, ci_gate, autouse_fixture, and test_helper is left unstated, yet AC1's pairwise-disjointness partition and the baseline key `<kind>::<name>` both depend on a determinate name per site — especially ci_gate, which draws from two distinct sources (scripts/check_*.py filenames AND workflow run: steps).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0c112bf20aee4c09","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Name.' paragraph and the live-counts table","norm_id":"nc96763ac238632c4","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must invent a naming scheme for a lock class vs a .lock literal, or for a workflow run step vs a check script, to build the baseline keys","Two workflow run: steps with identical command text collapse to one entry (the same collision the plan warns about for config_key)"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a 'name derivation' column to the live-counts table: e.g. lock -> class name or literal path; ci_gate -> `script:<path>` for check scripts and `workflow:<file>::<step-name>` for run: steps; autouse_fixture -> `<module>::<funcname>`; test_helper -> file path; env_var -> the REBAR_* token.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim"